# ============ Runtime output (added 2026-10-16 — blocker I5 / B1) ============
# 30 runtime logs were committed because the intended rules lived in
# `Java.gitignore` — a filename git never reads. The rules are merged here and
# that decoy file was deleted in the same commit.
logs/
*.log
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# ============ Build output ============
# 61 MB fat jar at the repository root. The Dockerfile builds its own copy from
# target/*.jar (`COPY --from=builder /app/target/*.jar app.jar`), so the
# committed binary was pure churn. It is untracked, NOT deleted from disk.
# NOTE: never add a bare `*.jar` rule here — it would override the
# `!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar` negation on line 3 and break `mvnw` on a
# fresh clone.
/app.jar

